1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
Templates, and static files.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:10,923
Four episodes in, and the front of our site still shows Wagtail's welcome page.

3
00:00:10,923 --> 00:00:15,000
A teal egg, and welcome to your new Wagtail site.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,248
Today, it goes.

5
00:00:17,048 --> 00:00:23,278
It lives in an include, and Wagtail tells you in a comment that it is disposable.

6
00:00:23,278 --> 00:00:28,431
So we delete the include, the welcome template, and its stylesheet.

7
00:00:28,431 --> 00:00:29,738
Three files gone.

8
00:00:30,538 --> 00:00:33,768
Remember the rule from episode two.

9
00:00:33,768 --> 00:00:37,552
Model name, lowercased, with underscores.

10
00:00:37,552 --> 00:00:43,828
Home page becomes home_page.html, and you never wire it up anywhere.

11
00:00:43,828 --> 00:00:46,228
Wagtail just looks for it.

12
00:00:47,028 --> 00:00:52,181
And there are two places templates can live, both switched on in settings.

13
00:00:52,181 --> 00:00:57,404
App dirs finds templates inside each app, which is where page templates go.

14
00:00:57,404 --> 00:01:01,583
And the dirs setting points at the project templates folder,

15
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:05,622
which is where base.html lives, because every app uses it.

16
00:01:06,422 --> 00:01:07,653
Open base.html.

17
00:01:07,653 --> 00:01:11,592
The head that Wagtail generated is already good.

18
00:01:11,592 --> 00:01:15,120
An SEO title with a fallback, the user bar,

19
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:19,633
and that preview panel fix we looked at in episode two.

20
00:01:19,633 --> 00:01:20,864
Keep all of it.

21
00:01:20,864 --> 00:01:23,408
We are only replacing the body.

22
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:29,124
A header, a main, and a footer, wrapped around the content block.

23
00:01:29,124 --> 00:01:31,015
That is the whole layout.

24
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:34,570
Every page in the series inherits it from here.

25
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:37,606
Three tags do all the linking.

26
00:01:37,606 --> 00:01:41,705
Page url takes a page object and gives you its address.

27
00:01:41,705 --> 00:01:44,164
Slug url looks a page up by slug,

28
00:01:44,164 --> 00:01:50,201
which is why the brand link keeps working even if somebody renames the home page.

29
00:01:50,201 --> 00:01:54,598
And the rich text filter turns a rich text field into HTML.

30
00:01:54,598 --> 00:01:58,548
All three need the wagtail core tags load at the top.

31
00:01:59,348 --> 00:02:03,855
And this is where last episode's warning pays off.

32
00:02:03,855 --> 00:02:07,011
Never build a link out of url path.

33
00:02:07,011 --> 00:02:10,617
It gives you/home/about, which is a 404.

34
00:02:10,617 --> 00:02:13,862
Page url gives you the real address.

35
00:02:14,662 --> 00:02:18,994
And here is the page tree finally doing something useful.

36
00:02:18,994 --> 00:02:21,807
The home page lists its own children.

37
00:02:21,807 --> 00:02:25,075
It does not know that an About page exists.

38
00:02:25,075 --> 00:02:26,747
It just asks the tree.

39
00:02:26,747 --> 00:02:32,296
Dot live means published pages only, so drafts stay hidden from visitors.

40
00:02:33,096 --> 00:02:34,603
Now the styling.

41
00:02:34,603 --> 00:02:40,539
Wagtail generates a stylesheet at studio/static/css/studio.css,

42
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:45,626
links it in base.html, and leaves it completely empty.

43
00:02:45,626 --> 00:02:46,663
Zero bytes.

44
00:02:46,663 --> 00:02:49,395
We fill it in with plain CSS.

45
00:02:49,395 --> 00:02:56,178
No build step, no framework, not in this episode and not in any of them.

46
00:02:56,978 --> 00:03:01,630
The static tag turns a path inside your static folder into a URL,

47
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:05,853
using the static files dirs setting we read in episode two.

48
00:03:05,853 --> 00:03:08,788
In development the server just serves it.

49
00:03:08,788 --> 00:03:14,156
In production there is a collect static step, and that is episode thirteen.

50
00:03:14,956 --> 00:03:21,472
And now the thing that will cost you ten minutes, because it cost me ten minutes.

51
00:03:21,472 --> 00:03:22,920
You write the CSS.

52
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:23,805
You reload.

53
00:03:23,805 --> 00:03:27,184
And the page is still completely unstyled.

54
00:03:27,184 --> 00:03:29,758
Nothing is wrong with your code.

55
00:03:30,558 --> 00:03:31,914
Here is the proof.

56
00:03:31,914 --> 00:03:37,035
The stylesheet is attached to the page, but it has zero rules in it.

57
00:03:37,035 --> 00:03:43,135
Meanwhile fetching the same URL returns two thousand bytes of perfectly good CSS.

58
00:03:43,135 --> 00:03:44,566
The server is fine.

59
00:03:44,566 --> 00:03:48,934
Your browser cached that file back when it was zero bytes,

60
00:03:48,934 --> 00:03:51,720
and it is still using the empty copy.

61
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,405
The fix is a hard reload.

62
00:03:54,405 --> 00:03:58,553
Control F five on Windows, or command shift R on a Mac.

63
00:03:58,553 --> 00:04:02,324
Every single person following along will hit this,

64
00:04:02,324 --> 00:04:08,584
because the file ships empty and you loaded the site before you wrote anything into

65
00:04:08,584 --> 00:04:08,810
it.

66
00:04:09,610 --> 00:04:10,930
And there it is.

67
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:14,890
A header, a title, the intro from episode three,

68
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:19,840
a list of child pages generated from the tree, and a footer.

69
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:21,820
That is our studio site.

70
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:25,641
The About page gets the same layout for free,

71
00:04:25,641 --> 00:04:28,460
because it extends the same base template.

72
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:31,749
And that back link is built from page.get_parent,

73
00:04:31,749 --> 00:04:36,246
so it always points at wherever the page actually sits in the tree.

74
00:04:37,046 --> 00:04:40,808
And one media query makes it work on a phone.

75
00:04:40,808 --> 00:04:46,324
At 375 pixels the heading drops from two point six rem to two rem.

76
00:04:46,324 --> 00:04:50,504
That is the entire responsive story for this site.

77
00:04:51,304 --> 00:04:52,563
One last thing.

78
00:04:52,563 --> 00:04:57,765
If you try a bad URL you still get Django's yellow debug page.

79
00:04:57,765 --> 00:05:01,541
The 404 template exists and extends our base,

80
00:05:01,541 --> 00:05:05,821
but Django only uses it when debug is switched off.

81
00:05:05,821 --> 00:05:08,842
That is episode thirteen, not a bug.

82
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:12,156
Commit, and tag.

83
00:05:12,956 --> 00:05:15,317
Our pages look like a site now,

84
00:05:15,317 --> 00:05:19,430
but the body field is still one big blob of rich text.

85
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:24,229
Next episode, StreamField replaces it with real content blocks.

86
00:05:24,229 --> 00:05:28,190
That is the episode most people come to Wagtail for.

87
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:34,190
Next episode, StreamField.

88
00:05:34,190 --> 00:05:38,190
Thanks for watching.
